@startuml activity-note-page-decision
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the note-page decision is a decision table evaluated in order (first match wins),
'' split between what the first paint decides synchronously and the work it leaves for a background task that walks
'' page text — two owners, one pure and one effectful. Activity swimlanes show the owner of each step, `elseif`
'' chains render the table in its exact order, and <latex> labels set the label rules as mathematics; the fills come
'' from the shared theme and the SVG renders byte-reproducibly (README §4). Lanes and fills, from the shared
'' palette: orange = the pure notes model (vinary.slides.notes), the "model orange" of the pure libraries;
'' teal = the renderer side that reads page text with pdf.js and adopts the result (vinary.slides.evidence/settle,
'' renderer.pdf); red = a decision that shows the deck as it is (no page hidden), the error/refusal hue.
!include _vv-theme.iuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on

title Which pages of a Beamer deck are note pages (ADR-0048 §2)

|#F5EAE0|first paint · the pure notes model (notes/initial, plan)|
start
:the evidence — page labels <latex>L_0, \dots, L_{n-1}</latex>, the Producer,
the page sizes — and the parsed pdfpc sidecar;  <<IR_TINT>>
if (a second-screen axis (doubled pages,\nor pdfpc's notes position)?) then (yes)
  :split notes: the other half is the slide;  <<IR_TINT>>
  stop
elseif (not a Beamer source?) then (yes)
  ::not-beamer;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  stop
elseif (one page?) then (yes)
  ::one-page;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  stop
elseif (no page labels (one XeLaTeX pass)?) then (yes)
  if (<latex>n > 2000</latex>?) then (yes)
    ::too-many-pages;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :pending **:scan**;  <<IR_TINT>>
  endif
elseif (a label that is not a\nnon-negative integer?) then (yes)
  ::labels-not-integers;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  stop
else (integer labels)
  :**interleaving** — the label automaton, gap by gap: a page <latex>j \ge 1</latex>
  with <latex>L_j = j + 1</latex> may be a note page; every other page is a
  required slide; the valid parses are one choice per gap (§2.1);  <<IR_TINT>>
  if (:proven — one valid parse, with note pages?) then (yes)
    if (the Producer is pdfTeX / LuaTeX / LuaHBTeX\nand the labels are not restartable?) then (yes)
      :**the note pages are hidden at once**
      (proof [:labels]);  <<IR_TINT>>
      stop
    elseif (the confirmation would read\nmore than 2 000 pages?) then (yes)
      ::too-many-pages;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
      stop
    else (no)
      :pending **:confirm**;  <<IR_TINT>>
    endif
  elseif (:ambiguous — several parses, only in the plain run,\n<latex>L_0 \le 1</latex>, distinct first note pages?) then (yes)
    :pending **:probe** (and :confirm after it
    unless the Producer is trusted);  <<IR_TINT>>
  else (:none · :invalid · :undecidable)
    ::no-note-pages · :invalid · :undecidable;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
    stop
  endif
endif
|#E3F2ED|background · page text over pdf.js (evidence/settle), adopted by renderer.pdf|
:after the first frame, once per document version —
the deck is shown as it is until this decides;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
if (pending :scan?) then (yes)
  :every page in order: a note page when its signature
  (SIG — a scaled copy of the last slide's text, <latex>\sigma \le 0.4</latex>,
  half its characters) matches the last slide before it;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  if (note pages found?) then (yes)
    :hidden (proof [:scan]);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  else (no)
    ::no-note-pages;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  endif
elseif (pending :probe?) then (yes)
  :walk the candidates from the LAST: the pair <latex>(a - 1, a)</latex>
  passes SIG → candidate <latex>a</latex>; fails but page <latex>a</latex> carries the
  rotated date → the previous candidate; else the parse with no
  note page in the plain run, when it is valid;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  if (a parse with note pages?) then (yes)
    if (trusted Producer?) then (yes)
      :hidden (proof [:labels :probe]);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
    else (no)
      :CONFIRM, as below → [:labels :probe :confirm]
      or :confirm-failed;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
    endif
  else (none valid · none with note pages)
    ::probe-undecided · :no-note-pages;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  endif
else (pending :confirm)
  :CONFIRM — every note page <latex>j</latex> passes SIG against the
  slide it annotates, or carries the rotated date;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  if (all confirmed?) then (yes)
    :hidden (proof [:labels :confirm]);  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
  else (no)
    ::confirm-failed;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
  endif
endif
:an unreadable page → :unreadable · anything unexpected → :error ·
more than 2 000 pages read → :too-many-pages — each shows the deck
as it is; a document closed meanwhile gets nothing applied.
Every view still showing that version adopts the result;  <<RENDERER_TINT>>
stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Swimlane / concept |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the pure notes model, at the first paint (vinary.slides.notes) |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the background work over page text, and the views that adopt it |
  |<#E0211D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| a reason: no page is hidden, the deck is shown as it is |
  SIG compares two pages' text runs (§2.2). Beyond the bounds of 4 096 runs and
  65 536 code units a page, and 16 384 matches a pair, it gives "no evidence".
endlegend
@enduml
